<template>
    <heading>Operations</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>operations</li>
        <li>generator</li>
        <li>coroutine</li>
        <li>event handler</li>
        <li>initialization</li>
        <li>to_handler</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p>Operations hold the application's multi-step event handlers. Each handler is a generator object, created and primed by <code>to_handler</code>. The generator receives a function that returns its own object; calling that function after construction avoids accessing the object before it exists.</p>
        <p>The base handler receives events and ignores them for now. It yields itself to remain the current handler. Operations install the primed base handler with <code>controller.init</code> before any events are dispatched.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>Outermost scope objects</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
let operations = (() => {
    function to_handler(generator) {
        const handler = generator(() => handler);
        handler.next();
        return handler;
    }

    function* baseOperationsHandler(self) {
        while (true) {
            let event = yield self();
        }
    }

    const handler = to_handler(baseOperationsHandler);
    controller.init(handler);

    return {};
})();
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
